 "caveats": [
  "covarying (mzLib's PtmPairEngine.CoVarying, type A): Spearman's rho of two sites' occupancies across runs, on the runs where both are quantified. Floors and not_detected cells are not values and are left out, and so, unless --keep-ceiling, are ceilings: two unrelated sites both read 1 in low-load runs, which would correlate them through detection alone. --include-bounds enters them as tied bounds instead.",
  "A site enters co-varying pairs only if it is quantified in at least min_quantified_fraction of covarying_run_count, the runs (or samples) where any site was identified or covered.",
  "q is Benjamini-Hochberg within fdr_family (the type, then intra or inter protein). An overlapping pair, two sites one peptide covers, is reported but left out of the family (q null): shared peptides correlate it by construction. q is not a target-decoy q-value.",
  "p_value is Spearman's two-sided p, exact for 9 or fewer runs without ties, otherwise asymptotic (t on n - 2 degrees of freedom), as stats correlate reports it.",
  "With --run-covariate, rho and p_value are the partial Spearman correlation given each run's target_psms (with --remove-run-level, given both). It is ranked like every variable, so any increasing transform of it, such as log2, gives the same result. Shallow runs make covered-zeros co-occur across unrelated sites, which a depth covariate takes out. A run with no value is left out of every pair, and a pair sharing fewer than 10 runs is not tested (test_status too_few_shared_runs).",
  "The observations follow ptmqtl occupancy's rules: MS/MS identifications only, one row per (run, peptidoform, protein), and the same exclusions (Common Variable, Common Fixed, peptide-terminal and C-terminal modifications)."
 ]
}
